    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d63">

                <pb facs="0074" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg64"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/5–1848</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Koo</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <p>The Chinese Ambassador presents his compliments to the Secretary of State and has
                    the honor to refer to the Memorandum of the Department of May 7, 1948,
                    transmitting a List from the Department of the Air Force which indicates the
                    status of availability in the stocks of the United States Air Force of items of
                    equipment for Mosquito aircraft.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador will appreciate it if the Secretary would be good enough to inform
                    the Department of the Air Force and the Office of the Foreign Liquidation
                    Commissioner that the Chinese Government desires to acquire all the items shown
                    in the List as available and that a representative of the Washington Office of
                    the Chinese Air Force will contact the Commissioner for this purpose.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador wishes to take this opportunity to thank the Department of the Air
                    Force for its valuable suggestion as regards the suitability of the desired 20
                    mm guns for the Mosquito aircraft.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-05-18">May 18, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
